      {id:"controller_scan",title:"Capture controller faults and event data",instruction:"Scan all relevant OEM-designated controllers. Record exact fault identifiers, source controller, active/inactive status, occurrence information and freeze-frame/event data. Separate primary faults from possible consequences before selecting a system.",test:"Complete controller scan, DTC status, occurrence count, source controller and freeze-frame/event data",prompt:"Attach the complete scan report and record controller, exact code, status and event data. If an active fault has a code-specific guided path, use it before continuing generic triage.",choices:["Relevant active fault(s) identified; not yet reviewed","Active faults reviewed; no primary cause established","Only inactive / historic faults","Multiple unrelated faults; primary not identified","No relevant faults found after complete scan","Scan incomplete / controller not communicating"]},
      {id:"data_review",title:"Compare live data with the correct specification",instruction:"Choose data that directly relates to the complaint. Record commanded and actual values, units, operating conditions and source controller. Compare only with specifications for the exact engine, emissions level and calibration.",test:"Complaint-related commanded/actual live data, sensor plausibility and applicable OEM specifications",prompt:"Select only parameters that can discriminate between likely systems. Record units, test conditions, source controller and exact OEM limit; do not apply generic thresholds.",choices:["Data points toward a specific subsystem","Data is implausible or inconsistent","Values appear within applicable specification","More data or vehicle information required"]},
      {id:"targeted_inspection",title:"Narrow the system and inspect supporting evidence",instruction:"Use the complaint, fault data and measurements to select the next focused system. Inspect only the supported subsystem and document the physical or measured evidence before identifying a cause.",test:"One focused OEM pinpoint test or physical inspection for the supported subsystem",prompt:"Use the correct dedicated workflow and vehicle-specific OEM procedure. Record the test point, measurement, physical evidence and source; do not replace a component from a broad symptom.",choices:["Specific subsystem isolated for focused diagnosis","Physical evidence found; cause not yet confirmed","No subsystem isolated","Vehicle-specific information still needed"]},
      {id:"triage_verify",title:"Document findings and next diagnostic direction",instruction:"Record what the evidence supports, what remains unknown and the next focused test or workflow. Do not label a component failed without a confirming test and applicable specification.",test:"Confirmed diagnostic direction, supporting evidence and next OEM test/workflow",prompt:"Name the subsystem and the next specific diagnostic path. Preserve unresolved questions and measurements; this triage workflow is not a component-replacement authorization.",choices:["Focused diagnostic direction established","More evidence required","Complaint not reproduced; follow-up needed"],terminal:true}
